{"name":"Monastir","hex":"#b78999","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Monastir","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Bitola in North Macedonia."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A commune of Sardinia, Italy.","A coastal city in Tunisia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Monastir"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monastir, Tunisia","blocks":[{"text":"Monastir, also called Mestir, is a city on the central coast of Tunisia, in the Sahel area, some 20 kilometres south of Sousse and 162 kilometres south of Tunis. Traditionally a fishing port, Monastir is now a major tourist resort. Its population is about 93,306. It is the capital of Monastir Governorate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/View_of_Monastir_from_the_ribat_tower.jpg/330px-View_of_Monastir_from_the_ribat_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monastir%2C_Tunisia","wikidata":"Q208715"},{"title":"Monastir Habib Bourguiba International Airport","blocks":[{"text":"Monastir Habib Bourguiba International Airport is an airport serving Monastir and Sousse areas in Tunisia. The Tunisian Civil Aviation and Airports Authority (OACA) awarded the management of the airport to TAV Airports Holding in March 2007. The airport is named after former president Habib Bourguiba (1903–2000), who was born in Monastir."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Monastir_airport.jpg/330px-Monastir_airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monastir_Habib_Bourguiba_International_Airport","wikidata":"Q666704"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Monastir_from_space.jpg/500px-Monastir_from_space.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/